    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Power of lens (P = 1/f in metres): Power is negative for Myopia (concave lens) and positive for Hypermetropia (convex lens).",
        "Planets do not twinkle because they are closer to Earth and act as an extended array of point sources, nullifying the atmospheric variation effect.",
        "Red light is scattered the least by air molecules due to its longer wavelength, making it ideal for danger and stop signals.",
        "Presbyopia occurs due to the gradual weakening of ciliary muscles and decreasing flexibility of the eye lens with aging, corrected by bifocal lenses."
      ],
      "id": "jxksq6i"
